{"skill":{"slug":"monitoring","displayName":"Monitoring"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770919741223,"changelog":"Initial release","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2805,"sha256":"6ad765fdd5f46959a76bf62cbdc47fe37430e364c03143d3886524b522a6ac63","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"alerting.md","size":4434,"sha256":"3e490de9af0e3b683a9054268f7443d6d72a69fba921fe558dbbb047815bc924","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"apm.md","size":3623,"sha256":"b930ac6d71445dfddae2f3011040fee809d80283799c5e7675c19bd2bbeaf062","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"logs.md","size":3980,"sha256":"c4c4b6fdf6cc9e33ce4f77503122182f342e1598b18b4fb9d9245b62092b4251","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"prometheus.md","size":5274,"sha256":"6d58110fd907ab296150ded805c246b6d99204a35d20d98e6291fc3e8909d750","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"simple.md","size":2312,"sha256":"da0ae0040328dd898850c57891bdad0ba99524b401a31f9c36a162442bc549ec","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2521,"sha256":"afde3df575ab9f926140cd5bc4c89bf1f3169c1d848bc276c74fcc8a4b9f3230","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789063850815,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"66bf5df994bb63c23a480ea9f5d14d854f63f2cdca64d965460e2ebc4a835ca4","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/66bf5df994bb63c23a480ea9f5d14d854f63f2cdca64d965460e2ebc4a835ca4","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: monitoring\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill bundle for 'monitoring' is benign. It provides comprehensive documentation and setup instructions for legitimate observability tools (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, Sentry, Uptime Kuma). While it includes commands to fetch and execute remote code (e.g., `npm install`, `npx`, `docker run`) and configure services that handle sensitive data (e.g., DSNs, API keys, passwords), these are standard practices for deploying and configuring monitoring software. There is no evidence of prompt injection, data exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or obfuscation beyond the legitimate scope of setting up an observability stack.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779163525125},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":32,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789063850815},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is documentation-only and aligned with monitoring, but several examples would deploy persistent monitoring services, expose host telemetry, or run unpinned third-party installers without enough safety guidance.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The Prometheus examples bind services to host ports and mount /proc, /sys, and the host root filesystem read-only for node_exporter without warning users about host visibility or network exposure.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill package itself is markdown-only, but its setup instructions tell users to run unpinned remote installers or images, including npx @sentry/wizard@latest and louislam/uptime-kuma:1.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The guidance includes production-like commands that publish monitoring ports, collect logs/traces, log user identifiers and IP addresses, and export telemetry, but it gives little scoping, redaction, access-control, or compliance guidance.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Persistent Docker services, restart policies, and volumes are expected for monitoring, but users should explicitly control where they run and expose them.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is observability setup, and the artifacts consistently provide metrics, logs, traces, alerting, and monitoring guidance; the sensitive behaviors are mostly purpose-aligned.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review and harden the examples before installing anything: pin package and image versions, avoid running remote installers casually, bind monitoring ports to localhost or private networks, require authentication/TLS/firewall rules, restrict host mounts, redact logs and traces, and keep alert messages free of secrets or sensitive operational details.","findings":"[RP1] expected: The Sentry wizard command fits APM setup, but using @latest means users may execute changed remote code without review.\n[SQP-2] expected: APM collection of stack traces, breadcrumbs, user context, and exported traces is normal for observability, but the artifact does not adequately cover minimizing or redacting sensitive telemetry.\n[SQP-2] expected: Structured logging examples are relevant, but direct user IDs, IP addresses, and debug request payload guidance need stronger privacy and secret-redaction warnings.\n[SQP-2] expected: node_exporter host mounts are a common host-metrics pattern, but mounting /proc, /sys, and / should be explicitly framed as trusted-environment host visibility.\n[RP1] expected: The Uptime Kuma Docker command is relevant to simple monitoring, but the mutable major-version tag weakens reproducibility and reviewability.\n[SQP-2] expected: Telegram alerts are a plausible notification channel, but the artifact should warn that alert contents may be shared with a third-party messaging service.\n[T03] expected: The static finding is supported for the unpinned Sentry npx command; it is a supply-chain and execution-risk concern, not evidence of malicious intent by itself.\n[T09] expected: The static finding is supported where Loki, Prometheus, Grafana, and Alertmanager ports are published without accompanying authentication, TLS, firewall, or localhost-binding guidance.\n[T08] expected: The static finding is supported for the mutable Uptime Kuma image tag; the command is purpose-aligned but should be pinned and reviewed.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789063850815}}}}}